  "answer": "## Issue summary\n\nYou’re pointing out an inconsistency in MUI’s spacing-to-CSS mapping for `sx`:\n\n- `sx={{ padding: 2, margin: 2 }}` follows the spacing rule (theme spacing → typically `2` ⇒ `theme.spacing(2)`).\n- But logical properties like `sx={{ paddingInlineStart: 2 }}` end up being treated as a **raw pixel value** (`2px`) instead of using the spacing scale (`theme.spacing(2)` ⇒ typically `16px` with default theme).\n\n## What’s missing from the provided excerpts\n\nThe wiki excerpts you provided do **not** include any of the core implementation that converts `sx`/style values into CSS (e.g., the `spacing` transformer, `Box`/`sx` system functions, or the logic that distinguishes physical vs logical `padding*`/`margin*` properties). The only code body present is unrelated (`packages/mui-docs/src/svgIcons/TypeScript.js`). Therefore, there’s nothing in the provided material I can cite to confirm where the logical property mapping currently happens or how to change it.\n\n## Likely intended behavior (based on the issue text)\n\nPer your expectation:\n\n- All `padding`/`margin` values should use `theme.spacing(...)`.\n- Special case currently exists for:\n  - `padding{Inline/Block}{Start/End}`\n- That case should instead also resolve `2` using `theme.spacing(2)` rather than assuming pixel units.\n\n## Next step (what I’d look for in-repo)\n\nTo implement/fix this, you’d search for the `sx` style value resolution for spacing, and specifically where `paddingInlineStart`/`paddingInlineEnd`/`paddingBlockStart`/`paddingBlockEnd` are normalized. Look for code in the `sx`/style system layer (e.g., something like a “spacing function” or “style property value normalizer”) and adjust it so these logical properties follow the same spacing token handling as `padding`/`margin`.",
